.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dfdu-export 1  "dfdu-export " 
.SH NAME
dfdu\-export \- Scan a directory and write it in ncdu\*(Aqs JSON format
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdfdu export\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-compress\fR] [\fB\-\-snapshot\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-resume\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\-agent\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR] [\fB\-\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-mft\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan a directory and write it in ncdu\*(Aqs JSON format
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR [default: \-]
Where to write (`\-` for stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-compress\fR
Compress with zstd (ncdu reads it with `\-f`; dfdu recognises it on import)
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshot\fR
Write dfdu\*(Aqs own snapshot format instead (lossless, checked, compressed; for `dfdu \-f` and `\-\-resume\-from`, not for ncdu)
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Worker threads
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\-from\fR \fI<SNAPSHOT>\fR
Start from this snapshot (`\-\-snapshot`) and rescan only the directories changed since it was taken, when the volume\*(Aqs change journal can tell (macOS, Windows, btrfs as root); otherwise everything. PATH and the mount options are the snapshot\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<HOST>\fR
Scan PATH on this host, through ssh; the dfdu agent is sent there if it has none (\-\-remote\-agent)
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\-agent\fR \fI<HOW>\fR
How to start the agent on HOST: auto (an installed dfdu that speaks this one\*(Aqs protocol, else one sent earlier, else send this version\*(Aqs, asking first), installed, or upload (send one without asking) [default: auto, or DFDU_REMOTE_AGENT]
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: The installed dfdu if it speaks this one\*(Aqs protocol, else one sent earlier, else send one (asking first)
.IP \(bu 2
installed: The dfdu installed on the host, as `ssh HOST dfdu agent`
.IP \(bu 2
upload: One sent earlier, else send one, without asking
.RE
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR
Stay on the filesystem of the scanned directory (the default; overrides \-\-cross\-mounts and \-\-network given before it)
.TP
\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR
Descend into other local filesystems (disks, tmpfs)
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR
Descend into network filesystems (NFS, SMB, sshfs and other FUSE network mounts); with or without \-\-cross\-mounts
.TP
\fB\-\-mft\fR
Windows, as administrator: read each NTFS volume\*(Aqs master file table instead of listing its directories, which is much faster on large volumes. Volumes whose table cannot be read are listed as usual
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

